WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.368
Hello, I'm Camille.

2
00:00:02.718 --> 00:00:06.870
Today: the fake bank adviser scam, one of the costliest scams around.

3
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.898
Your phone rings. The screen shows your bank's number.

4
00:00:11.248 --> 00:00:15.224
On the line, a calm voice tells you there are suspicious payments on your account.

5
00:00:15.924 --> 00:00:22.140
To “block” the fraud, you are asked to read out a code received by text, or to approve an operation in your banking app.

6
00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.538
But that code blocks nothing: it approves a payment.

7
00:00:25.888 --> 00:00:28.456
And that payment goes straight to the scammer.

8
00:00:29.156 --> 00:00:30.780
There are other versions.

9
00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.594
You may be asked to transfer your money to a so-called safe account.

10
00:00:34.944 --> 00:00:37.624
Or to hand your card to a courier who comes to your home.

11
00:00:37.974 --> 00:00:40.590
Or to install an app that gives access to your phone.

12
00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:47.042
Remember just one thing: your bank will never ask you to approve an operation in order to cancel it.

13
00:00:47.392 --> 00:00:51.544
If in doubt, hang up, and call back yourself on the number on the back of your card.

14
00:00:52.244 --> 00:00:54.972
If you've already been caught out, act fast.

15
00:00:55.322 --> 00:01:04.650
Block your card straight away, using your banking app or the number on the back of your card. In the UK, you can also call 159 to reach your bank safely.

16
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.184
Call your bank on its usual number.

17
00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:12.822
Then report the fraud: to Report Fraud in the UK, or to the FTC in the US.

18
00:01:13.522 --> 00:01:16.138
Remember: two safeguards are better than one.

19
00:01:16.488 --> 00:01:19.368
That was Camille, for Prometis. See you soon!
